  "operative_text": "Section 1 (SDCL 23-7-7.1): A temporary permit to carry a concealed pistol shall be issued within five days of application to a person if the applicant: (1) Is eighteen years of age or older; (2) Is not prohibited by South Dakota law from possessing a firearm; (3) Has never pled guilty to, nolo contendere to, or been convicted of a crime of violence as defined by subdivision 22-1-2(9); A person denied a permit may appeal to the circuit court pursuant to chapter 1-26."
